			<abstract>
				<p>In the era of big data and AI, recommender systems must adapt to evolving user preferences and new users/items to maintain highquality recommendations. Fine-tuning, which updates model parameters using only new data, offers an efficient alternative to full retraining but struggles to balance stability (retaining past knowledge) and plasticity (adapting to new knowledge). While existing CCS Concepts • Information systems → Data mining; • Computing methodologies → Machine learning.</p>
